# Make overflow and collision correction visual

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical notes describe current implementation evidence and gaps. The
finite acceptance below does not imply those gaps were implemented.

Draw page-edge, collision, and unsupported-mode diagnostics on preview and link
each overlay to the owning source object and correction actions.

## Finite three-class visual diagnostic and correction contract

**Inputs:** one accepted revision/page with stable semantic object IDs,
current complete backend diagnostic evidence, measured page/object geometry,
and the requested output capability. **Outputs:** a preview overlay linked
to its owning source object and a typed candidate correction, or a visible
incomplete/unresolved result. An overlay alone has no mutation, file Export,
or physical-plan authority.

**Presentation rule:** render a bounded overlay for one current diagnostic
per class: page-edge overflow, object collision and unsupported output mode.
Each overlay conveys its stable diagnostic identity, blocking disposition,
semantic owner, target page, relevant geometry and admitted correction
categories. Selection from the overlay focuses the same owner in the source
inspector. Never hide an error behind the drawing or imply a proposed remedy
has passed layout, source, or device capability checks.

**Worked three-class example:** writable page rectangle `x=20..190 mm`,
`y=20..277 mm`; fixed figure `f1` at `(184,40,12,20)` mm crosses right edge
by `6 mm`. A red-edge overlay identifies `f1` and proposes `move left 6 mm`,
subject to a new constraint check. Figure `f2` overlaps `f3` over a
`5 x 5 mm` measured region; the collision overlay identifies both semantic
owners and proposes a reviewed reposition rather than auto-shifting either.
Figure `f4` is a color photograph in single-pen live mode; its capability
overlay proposes a supported explicit line-art conversion request or a
Digital/PDF output choice, never silent monochrome substitution.

**Refusal example:** a diagnostic generated for revision `r5` must not
activate a correction in `r6`. An overlay lacking a stable owner, precise
geometry, supported remediation, or complete evidence must show
`UnresolvedDiagnostic` instead of claiming the page is ready. A proposed
move that removes right-edge overflow but creates a collision remains
blocking after fresh reevaluation; no preview gesture silently commits it.

**Assumptions and limits:** a read-only overflow diagnostic and layout-only
Export preflight are existing backend primitives. Collision measurement,
unsupported-mode diagnostics with consistent geometry, preview paint/hit-test,
selection sync and fully authorized correction commands are unfinished.
Theoretical acceptance does not claim the three overlays are implemented or
that corrections can be safely applied to physical output.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for existing fixed-overflow evidence only; theoretical
  for visual overlays, collision and unsupported-mode workflows, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** three typed overlay examples, owner/geometry/diagnostic
  invariants, conditional corrections and stale/unsupported refusal.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** rendered overlays, collision
  solver, physical capability UI, or end-to-end correction commands.
